module

public import LeanCategories.Lattices.Valued.FoldingEnriques

/-!
# Folding a Lorentzian chamber along a *diagram* involution (`#116`, stage 2)

`Folding.lean` folds a chamber along an abstract lattice involution: it defines the fixed
sublattice, the folded vector `α^J` of AEGS Definition 3.3, the folded root set, the folded
Coxeter diagram of a root family, and the cone identities (Lemma 3.8's two lines). This file
carries the **diagram** side of the same construction, which is what §3.8 of the source uses:

* **The diagram involution** (`ActsThrough`): a global isometry `g` of the lattice acts on a root
  family `r` through a permutation `π` of its index set. `actsThrough_involutive` recovers
  `π ∘ π = id` from `g * g = 1` and injectivity of `r`, `actsThrough_edges` shows `π` preserves
  the normalized pairing square of every pair, so `π` is an automorphism of the Coxeter diagram
  `G` of `r`, and `actsThrough_folded_eq` shows the folded vector is constant on the orbits of
  `π` — the source's "the folded diagram `G^J` has the vectors `α^J` … as vertices", one vertex
  per *orbit*, which is why the folded diagram is smaller than the diagram it comes from.
* **The walls of the folded chamber** (`rootMirror_folded_inter_fixed`,
  `rootMirrorCone_folded_iff`, `chamberOf_folded_trace_walls`): inside the invariant part
  `M^σ ⊗ ℝ` of the real form (`realFormFixedPart`, the fixed locus of the involution, not merely
  the image of the fixed lattice), the mirror section of a folded root is the mirror section of the
  root, and
  the folded root set is the wall set of the chamber that the root set cuts out
  (`IsChamberWithWalls`, `#23`). This is the content of AEGS Lemma 3.8 stated at the level it is
  proved there: the chamber `C^J := C ∩ T_En ⊗ R` is cut out by the folded simple roots, and its
  walls are the folded walls.
* **A worked folded diagram** (`tdpFoldedE8Diagram` and its edge computation): AEGS Lemma 3.9's
  statement "the sublattice `T^{J=1}_dP` is generated by the vectors `α_k + α_{20-k}`, `1 ≤ k ≤ 8`
  spanning `E₈(2)`", in the block model of `T_dP = U ⊕ U(2) ⊕ E₈ ⊕ E₈` of `FoldingEnriques.lean`.
  The eight `E₈` simple roots of the first summand are roots of `T_dP` of square `-2`
  (`tdpE8Root_square`), each is orthogonal to its image under `I = -I_En`
  (`tdpE8Root_pairing_image`), so each folds to a vector of square `-4` in the invariant
  sublattice (`tdpFoldedE8Root_square`, `tdpFoldedE8Root_mem_fixed`), and the folded diagram is
  the `E₈` diagram with every edge weight `1/4` — the doubled `E₈` diagram, `E₈(2)`
  (`tdpFoldedE8Diagram_edges`).

## What this file does *not* claim

`IsChamberWithWalls` for the invariant lattice `M^σ` itself is not stated, for the reason
`Folding.lean` records: its root-theoretic fields (`roots_mem`, `interior_regular`) need AEGS
Lemma 3.4's *converse*, the classification of the `(-2)`- and `(-4)`-vectors of the invariant
lattice up to the reflection group, which is an arithmetic input and not a consequence of
folding. What folding gives — and what is proved here — is that the folded roots are the walls of
the chamber in the invariant part, which is the second sentence of the lemma.

## References

* V. Alexeev, P. Engel, D. Z. Garza, L. Schaffler, *Compact moduli of Enriques surfaces with a
  numerical polarization of degree 2*, Nagoya Math. J. 259 (2025), arXiv:2312.03638v2, §3.7–3.8
  (Definition 3.3, Lemma 3.4, Definition 3.7, Lemma 3.8, Lemma 3.9, printed pp. 11–13).
* N. Bourbaki, *Lie Groups and Lie Algebras*, Ch. V §1, for chambers and their walls.
* E. B. Vinberg, *The groups of unit elements of certain quadratic forms*, Mat. Sb. 87 (1972), §1.

